  ('zcrm_1579374000173777009', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173762002', 'Tracy Fitzke', NULL, 'Member submitted payment update form.  I will process', 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2025-11-17 06:58:43', '2025-11-17 06:58:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173777001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173762002', 'Tracy Fitzke', 'Member Only $5000 IUA Secure HSA', NULL, 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2025-11-17 06:46:48', '2025-11-17 06:46:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173748001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000142862002', 'Victoria Shavlik', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 4507 Question : Why is my Cirrus MD accounts for myself and my son inactive?', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2025-11-15 10:20:17', '2025-11-15 10:20:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173728001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000073212091', 'Michelle Schusterman', 'Zoho SalesIQ chat missed', 'Visit ID : 4506 Question : Hi! I was wondering if my plan included weight loss programs.', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2025-11-15 07:12:13', '2025-11-15 07:12:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173672133', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173662002', 'Daphne Mosko', NULL, '11-14-25 Daphne came to me via Daniella Papi. She''s 41 and son is 9. She''s self-employed and lives in Boulder. She does manual osteopathic work as a holistic practitioner and describes it as seeing miracles and magic! She addresses the whole body and mind and spirit as well as the physical body. She recognizes the complete corruption of our medical system! She loves her work. She''s super healthy, no meds, no tobacco, etc. No need for wellness benefits. She chose Care+ $2500/$387, $125/$25. She''s dating Jeff Sidwell who found MPB through Wiley''s HSA site and is a member. Small world.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-14 22:00:47', '2025-11-14 22:00:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173672128', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173671001', 'Anne White', NULL, '11-14-25 She enrolled today for Jan. 1st start date. She''s all set to go!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-14 21:55:01', '2025-11-14 21:55:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173672098', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000163576188', 'Daniel McCarthy', NULL, '11-14-25 <br>For Mary, she currently has RMHP Valley Colorado Option Gold thru Connect for Health Colorado.  We want to continue with this for 2026.  Do we need to do anything or will it automatically continue for next year?  The current premium is $1,159.75 (not including any PTC).  I understand the ACA subsidies are currently planning to go away for people over the 400% FPL.  What will this plan cost us next year? <br><br>*** No, your plan was not one that could be auto-renewed. If you expect your income to remain at about $90K then the cheapest plan starts at $1327.75 which is RMHP <span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);"> </span>Valley Colorado Option Bronze with a $7500 deductible and $10,000 max out of pocket<span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);"> </span>. The RMHP Valley Colorado Option Gold thru Connect for Health Colorado will be<span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);"> </span>$1530.97  Please let me know what you''d like to do.  <br><br>*** Thanks, Wendy', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-14 19:30:57', '2025-11-14 19:30:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173672093', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447059', 'Florie Glusman', NULL, '11-14-25 Per Grok and having the same counselor each session, here''s what it says, "OurLiveDoc operates as a connector to a network of independent telemedicine providers. Users select available providers based on availability, specialty, and scheduling, similar to many on-demand telehealth services (e.g., Teladoc or Doctor on Demand). This means counselors are matched per session rather than assigned long-term, unless the user specifically requests and schedules follow-ups with the same provider."', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-14 19:08:00', '2025-11-14 19:08:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173672088', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173867018', 'Amanda Conroy', NULL, '11-14-25 Amanda is 40 and has twin girls who are 14. They live in PA, so Care+ is the only option bc she''s not sef-employed. Only W2 employment. She doesn''t do wellness stuff except mammogram. She will pay for that on her own. She looked into CHSM and it was going to be $3000K IUA or AUA at $422 a month and must go in network. We Share was $483 month with a $5K share amount and some other one $540 or $560 with a network. She likes the idea of Care+, no network and not paying for wellness items she won''t likely use. Care+ is $1000/$461, $2500/$364 for Dec. and $1250/$494, $2500/$387 for Jan. 2026. She wants to join for Dec. 1st and we have a meeting on Monday at 2:00 to complete the enrollment. She watched the video also. She knows about the $125/$25. I''ll send her info to read.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-14 15:38:28', '2025-11-14 15:38:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173672073', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000174963059', 'Laura Waldman', NULL, '11-14-25 Laura is paying $879.52 for her RMHP/UHC and says they''ve been a nightmare and aren''t paying much. She sees a neurologist, PCP group, etc. Sees:<br><span style="color:rgb(77, 77, 79);"><b>Brink, Janel Nicole (MD)</b></span><br><span style="color:rgb(77, 77, 79);"><b>Hatzidakis, Armodios Miltiadis (MD)</b></span><br><span style="color:rgb(77, 77, 79);"><b>Li, Thomas Min Huang (MD)</b></span><br><span style="color:rgb(77, 77, 79);"><b>Maa, Edward Hueitai</b></span><br><span style="color:rgb(77, 77, 79);"><b>She''ll call each dr. to see if they''ll still see her while only on Medicaid if she cancels her C4 plan. She even has her daughter on her C4 account for taxes meaning she''ll have to earn even more to get a tax credit which might not be realistic.</b></span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-14 15:03:43', '2025-11-14 15:03:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173699001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000071992038', 'Willa Bonzi', NULL, '11/14/25<br>Called to see what she could do for mental health. i let ehr know all of the options because she is considering gtting regular insurance too. need to talk to patti or someone to remind myself what happens when you have both. i know zion gets in line but i dont know exactly how it works. will email her monday when i have an answer for her to let her know<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-11-14 15:00:01', '2025-11-14 15:00:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173672060', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000174963059', 'Laura Waldman', NULL, '11-14-25 Laura is on the following and she just chose me as her broker for Dec. 1st onward. She might cancel this altogether and stick with Medicaid solely. It makes no sense to paying $850-$950 a month when she has Medicaid. She''s not earning much yet. She will call her Drs. to see if they will keep working with her while solely on Medicaid.<br><span><br></span><p style="background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);"><b>Enrolled member(s):</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);">Laura Waldman</span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><br></span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>RMHP Colorado Doctors Plan Colorado Option Gold</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Primary Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Specialist Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$1,875</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$8,700</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Urgent Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(22