  ('zcrm_1579374000173633001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173614001', 'Austin Johnson', 'Member Only $5000 IUA Secure HSA', NULL, 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2025-11-14 06:33:34', '2025-11-14 06:33:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173573770', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176273028', 'Dawson Wetlaufer', NULL, '<span style="">11-13-25 Dan Sorcinelli came to me via WWSRA and Cami Garrison.  Dan is the employer of Dawson Wetlaufer who is 26. Dan''s company is in OR. He plans to offer CARE+ to Dawson who is his only employee. Dawson is healthy, no pre-x. He watched the video and asked me all of his questions. He just did his first wellness check in 5 years before he gets booted off his parents'' great ins plan. He came out with a clean bill of health. He''s fine not including the wellness benefits. They are interested in Care+ $1250/$268. They are looking at a Dec or Jan start date. I forget. Remember to waive $100 fee as WWSRA member and use WWSRA site!</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-13 22:36:16', '2025-11-13 22:36:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173573747', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173889002', 'Joseph Weinstein', NULL, '11-13-25 Joseph was referred to me by Kath Erwin and also mentioned that he knows Jan. Lives in Truckee, CA and is 57. He''s healthy. His only things were injuries from long ago. He skis, bikes, paddleboards, etc. He''s self-employed as a LMFT mental health therapist and does not take insurance bc it took up 50% of his time to deal with the billing. He can see twice the # of patients without accepting ins. He did have melanoma over 5 years ago as of Sept. of 2025. He just got a clean bill of health from his doctor! No skin blemishes, nothing. Covered CA was $566 for Silver 73/$0 Ded. In 2026 it will be $1597 for Silver 70/30 and ded $5800. So, he would love other options. Secure HSA is the only option for CA at $1250/$448 and $125/$25. He''s thrilled. He did mention 2 bulging discs at the end of our conversation which he not worried about at all. He said they are 95% better and no plans of anything on that front other than to be 100%. He expects to make $70K for 2026 and the person he spoke with at Covered CA are telling him he won''t qualify for any APTC at all. He likes to travel and his happy this works internationally as well!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-13 22:16:36', '2025-11-13 22:16:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173573068', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000130802017', 'Bruce Maleski', NULL, '11-13-25 Sara is re-enrolling but had to choose Premium Care bc she doesn''t have any sort of self-employment income. Choosing $2500/$246 EO. She completed Bruce''s cancellation due to Medicare. We had him as the primary bc he was the one self-employed. She understands wellness is only mammogram and colonoscopy after a 6 month wait. She will need to pay cash for any additional in person well check. She scheduled the Welcome Call since her membership is a little different. It will be  a good reminder.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-13 19:22:07', '2025-11-13 19:22:07'),
