  ('zcrm_1579374000173079448', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061091836', 'Amber Donnell', NULL, '11-5-25 I sent Amber info for a vision plan.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 23:19:45', '2025-11-06 23:19:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079412', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173398002', 'Dave Carpenter', NULL, '11-6-25 Kim lives in CA but grew up in CO with Cory Nickerson. She and her husband are both self-employed in real estate and interior design. Kim is 60 and husband is 59. She''s having a tough time with her recent Birthday. They had a long time grandfathered plan with Anthem BCBS and finally had to go onto Covered CA last year. They now see how terrible those plans are and might have to pay money back in taxes since they earned more than expected. She''s done with that! Their daughter is 22 and home schooled. Kim hates Kaiser and wants Dr. choice. Husband Dave has a back problem right now so he might need to stay on Covered CA and have Kim and daughter on Secure HSA for CA 1095-C form.Her docter is Braunreuther and Sutter Health is showing that they accept the PHCS and Multiplan network. They are paying $2222 but fill cost is $4K! So, she can''t stomach that and really wants to switch.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 23:08:08', '2025-11-06 23:08:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079407', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173343075', 'Laurie Cox', NULL, '11-6-25 Laurie is a former client of Bev''s. She''s self-employed nurse practitioner. I called her back at 11:53 today.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 23:01:47', '2025-11-06 23:01:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079381', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000154481402', 'Oscar Stevenson', NULL, '11-6-25 I told Robin, Oscar''s wife, I needed her to login to Oscar''s account not realizing he was already my client. She came via Alyssa this tie and Andrea last year. But, Robin is the one who handles his affairs bc he''s a truck driver and on the road all the time. I will let her know I''m all set and we can proceed!<br>He had prostate cancer two years ago. They will be earning $104,000 a year so they don''t qualify for a subsidy. I gave her the estimated prices already. It will be  a huge price difference to them since they''re only paying about $200 now. He wants Dr. Andrew Sarka. Zip 80016. He''s with Cigna now. Husband is self-employed.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 22:43:52', '2025-11-06 22:46:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079376', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000134767002', 'Kara Weld', NULL, '11-6-25 Kara called to figure out what to do with her membership once HAB is done. I recommended Secure HSA and she upgraded for Jan. 1st. I walked her through the Change Form and she got to the confirmation page.  It will be $1070/$1250.<br>For her group for Immersion Research they really wanted to start for Nov., Dec. or Jan 2026 at the latest. But a company called High Mark who she works with through Gusto is telling her she definitely can''t cancel the company plan until April 1st which is their open enrollment period. She''s going to appeal to see if she can cancel but she''s succumbed to the April 1st date if all else fails. At that point she might have 10 people if they move to HA Co-Op. They are all excited to join. Her employees still have their current plan intact, so that won''t be a problem. We will see if anything changes before we reach April.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 22:34:09', '2025-11-06 22:34:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079368', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173376001', 'Daniel Rutschmann', NULL, '11-6-25 Daniel 46 and his wife Kathy 45 did a ton of research about Sedera and Zion before we talked. He''s also interested in a DPC such as Cloud Medical. He''s most interested in including HSA as well. When he researched Cloud Medical the Admin person recommended he speak with Leslie and it turns out to be MPB he was sent back to. OMG. Leslie managed to now have contact with Dr. Tusek recently. He was confused by some of the information Leslie gave him about deadlines for the membership. He thought he had to join by Dec. 1st to be part of some group. But, he just has to join by Dec. 1st to fund the HSA. However, he''s already funded his own HSA, so it''s a moot point.  Daniel and Kathy asked me a billion questions about MPB, Sedera, Zion, DPC, HSA, Cloud Medical and even Delta Dental  Basic and I will send him 1Dental to review. He worked with some other broker who suggested Delta Dental Basic for only $57 for his cleanings. He believes it will be cheaper than paying full price for their cleanings. Their DOB''s are 1/7/80 D and 1/12/79 K.  He called me back again and asked a few more questions after hours. I told him if he decides to go with Zion or Sedera directly to please let me know and I can help him with that as well. He understood. I think they will choose Secure HSA for the best benefits for their age and the best price since he really wants to fund the HSA. He might add Cloud Medical DPC as well. They are self-employed.  Wants to keep Dr. Mertz DDS who shows up in the Dental Access network.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 22:23:06', '2025-11-06 22:24:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079363', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173376001', 'Daniel Rutschmann', NULL, '11-4-25 Daniel and wife Kathy came to me via Lauren Stanko. Daniel was born in Germany and can''t fathom how crazy our healthcare system is. We will talk on Thursday.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 22:14:35', '2025-11-06 22:14:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079328', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173079333', 'Jesse Ivers', NULL, '11-4-25 Jesse came to me via WWSRA but he lives in WA state. So, I sent him to Karen to join HA Co-Op and he signed up with her. He''s 30 and healthy. Doesn''t want to pay the crazy rate in WA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 22:09:35', '2025-11-06 22:09:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079263', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000178071417', 'Benjamin Caillat', NULL, '11-5-25 Zeona 39 and Ben 46 were with LHS many years ago but don''t want to go back to LHS. They don''t have pre-x, no meds, no tobacco. They are both self-employed, they do wellness and skin check. They also like natural care such as chiro and massage. Ben needs a colonscopy some time soon. He did one 2 years ago and they found a few polyps, so he must go back next May. I explained how it will likely be considered diagnostic and he will have to pay the IUA first before costs are shared. They are interested in Secure HSA and want Dec. 1st start date. They have since decided to move forward and I have schedule a time to have Ben enroll them.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 21:51:27', '2025-11-06 21:51:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079248', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000059725045', 'Michelle Skellion', NULL, '11-4-25 Michelle is a massage therapist, self-employed. Her world has blown up the past few years with deaths in the family (I think that''s what she told me). I might have that wrong. She got bills from 2022 onward for wellness visits bc her sons DOB was wrong in the system. She knows it''s Planstin from Dec. 1st  2020-2024. Then is switched to ARM Jan. 1st 2025 onward. Planstin needs to see that her membership was active the entire time. Her membership changed Sept.1st  2022 but continued to be active wth Planstin the entire time. Patti called her back and she hopped on the phone to talk with Patti.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 21:44:29', '2025-11-06 21:44:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079243', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175064001', 'Mary Luna', NULL, '11-4-25 Mary Luna is looking for Jan. 1st and has a job starting at the YMCA. She is an alternate payee on her husband''s pension. She was hoping this would qualify her for Secure HSA but I confirmed from Patti that is does not indicate self-employment. She was with Kaiser. She wants her wellness visits, skin check, eye screening but NO on colonoscopy. She has Quantum Health which is Free and gives her discounts on supplements, virtual urgent care plus accident and critical illness care. She did have a basal cell spot removed. I explained about the need to be careful with skin stuff depending on what''s on her record. She has prescriptions for dry skin and takes GLP1 for weight which she''s paying cash for now. She already has a refill to last until the end of year. One was $200 and they next was $400 and it''s compounded which makes it tougher to obtain. She will need to pay that on her own still which she understands.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 21:38:03', '2025-11-06 21:56:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079233', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000063253037', 'Bobbi Georgeton', NULL, '10-30-25 Bobbi called to review options. She wants to  keep Dr. Jennifer Grodberg and Melissa Karch (Nutritionist).', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 21:32:16', '2025-11-06 21:32:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079228', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001881022', 'Carolyn Tabak', NULL, '11-6-25 Carolyn has Cobra until the end of March. She has migraines, so not a good idea for MPB. I think she''s with BVSD right now. She wants a plan with a low ded when the time comes.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 21:30:36', '2025-11-06 21:30:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079199', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173671001', 'Anne White', NULL, '10-30-25 Anne was referred by Julie Oldhman. I left a vm for her and will try her again.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 21:28:37', '2025-11-06 21:28:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079189', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000175212001', 'Julie Barker', NULL, '11-6-25 She wasn''t available for the time I proposed, so I''m awaiting if they next option will work for her.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 21:26:32', '2025-11-06 21:26:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079179', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000104398007', 'Estefania Luna', NULL, '10-30-25 Spoke with Estefania about the HMA FBI investigation. She was very happy I alerted her bc she was just about to sign up her husband. She had about $1000 in the account and only used it once for contacts or something like that. I will continue to keep her posted.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 21:21:16', '2025-11-06 21:21:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079164', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000163360001', 'Blythe Burge', NULL, '10-30-25 Buffy called bc she wants to go to her gyn for wellness and is having trouble finding a provider to accept PHCS or accept new patients. She would love to keep her dr. if possible. I told her to call MPB Concierge again and ask for help with navigating the system to get them to accept the card and/or negotiate rates since in remote area with limited options. Looks like she called.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 21:05:41', '2025-11-06 21:05:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079154', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000071157012', 'Kia Tolan', NULL, '10-30-25 Sent Kia information about maternity, dental and vision. I let her know the $2500 IUA for maternity. She''s been a member since 2021, so waiting period is long past. All set for now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 21:00:31', '2025-11-06 21:00:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079135', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000082058002', 'Andrea Andersson', NULL, '10-30-25 Andi has been all sorts of trouble with getting what she needs from MPB and Lyric. I coached her with different solutions and see from above she''s still having trouble. I will reach out. We also re-enrolled Finn into Care+ for 1/1/25 since he turns 26 1/8/25. He will pay $268/$1000. All set on that front.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 20:46:09', '2025-11-06 20:46:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079130', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000143461021', 'Julie Faucett', NULL, '10-29-25 Julie is 58 and Mark is 61. He builds homes and just sold a home and owes a bunch of $. Mark has a hypoactive thyroid. Julie had a gall bladder attack and had an ultrasound. She has a cyst on her liver. She had a complete hysterectomy. She needs a colonoscopy in a year or two. Mark uses tobacco. I let her know the massive limitations for Mark and te extra $75 on Premium Care. She''s looking at it now just for her $299/$1000 or $267/$1500. They could join SW instead with a $100 surcharge.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 20:33:19', '2025-11-06 20:33:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079081', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000152460004', 'Sharon Montini', NULL, '11-6-25 She just removed me as her broker. I called her immediately and left a vm. We''ll see if she replies.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 15:25:29', '2025-11-06 15:25:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079076', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000153586188', '(Boyce) Ben Ford', NULL, '11-6-25 Ben''s income will be about $38K. He left one job but is earning more at his other job. He''s getting a sizable subsidy. He was very happy with his plan. It''s the cheapest <span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);">plan aside from Kaiser. He''s pleased with</span> Anthem. His daughter is on CHP+.  I sent him a copy of the plan and # to call Anthem. I told him is vital to call and set up the payment again in 10 days or so. He understood.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-06 15:20:41', '2025-11-06 15:20:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173079071', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000153586188', '(Boyce) Ben Ford', NULL, '11-6-25 <br><p style="background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);"><b>Enrolled member(s):</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);">Boyce Ford</span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><br></span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Anthem Silver Pathway Essentials 5500 $0 Select Drugs</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Primary Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Specialist Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$950</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$2,900</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">25% (after deductible)</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Urgent Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><b>Payment required from:</b></span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(227, 246, 255);">01/01/26 - 12/31/26</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color