  ('zcrm_1579374000173040004', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000030826048', 'Trent Mullikin', 'Teams Msg from Wendy:', 'Juliet has given us the thumbs up to allow Trent Mullikin to be reinstated and active. Can you please run his payment method and let me know when it''s good to go? Thank you!<br><span><br></span>11/6/25-Pmt rerun member reinstated', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-11-06 07:12:21', '2025-11-06 07:12:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173036027', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012351133', 'Brian DeCamp', NULL, '(Green Side) Member submitted payment update form. I will process.', 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2025-11-06 07:04:06', '2025-11-06 07:13:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000173036012', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000172945006', 'Amanda Pereira', NULL, '11/5-I processed this New Enrollment and noticed that Member lives in CA and does not have a MEC.  Patti sent an email to Advisor, Christine Corsini that this Member was enrolled in Care + and lives in CA. (individual mandate state)<br>11/6- Christine Corsini replied to Patti that she wants to leave her where she is, in Care +.', 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2025-11-06 06:54:54', '2025-11-06 06:54:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172953059', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447059', 'Florie Glusman', NULL, '10-30-25 Florie wants alternative care options for her preventive care that was covered with HAB.  She also has 1 emp who might be a good fit for L-X bc she''s in urgent care all of the time, 1x per month. Florie also wants her therapist to be reimbursable cash pay. Not sure that exists right now. Her employees are Abigayle Bacchus and Kendall Reeves.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-05 21:40:27', '2025-11-06 21:18:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172953054', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000173666001', 'Angela Rothamp', NULL, '11-4-25 <span style="">Angie came to me via Kristy Barber. Her son is already a member. Angie watched the 9-minute video but needs something for her daughter who has hip dysplasia and needs hip surgery soon. She''s in college at Grand Canyon State as a student. She''s 20 and in AZ for school but CO for permanent residence. After we talked for about 30 min. she let me know her son is a member and enrolled through Kirk. She''s thinking of doing a joint membership with her son. I told her to do so via Kirk. For her daughter she needs a specific complex surgery that they want to get donw at Steadman''s Clinic in Vail. Daughter might qualify for Medicaid while her income is $1000 per month with a marketing job for a turf company. Work picks up in May onward at closer to $3K per month. But, if she has a hip surgery, she won''t be able to work and her income will remain low. Angie will call Steadman''s to see if they accept Medicaid. If not, she will join an ACA plan when she moves back to CO after the semester and get her on a C4 plan. I''ll help her at that point. She also let me know they have CHSM now but mentioned Medishare too. With Medishare she was told to mention private health sharing and by doing so, the price jumped up by $9K for a new Need! She was horrified that they are encouraging not to say self-pay and how much the price increased. Ins thorugh school is $8K per semester. They might keep that through April of 2026.</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-05 20:06:23', '2025-11-05 20:06:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172953049', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025756253', 'Robin Beck', NULL, '11-5-25 Left vm for Robin returning her call.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-05 19:44:55', '2025-11-05 19:44:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172993218', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000142598002', 'Heather Bingaman', NULL, '11-5-25 Heather asked many questions to get back on track with all things. She now feels a bit better about her Care+ membership. She wants to upgrade to Secure HSA and may start her own bracelet business that she''s wanted to do for a long time. This will be good for kids camps and such to show proof of ins. She really has the most expenses with dental right now. I sent her the Delta Dental Classic Plan infor for $123 a month for 1 adult and 2 kids. She''s spending a ton on her kids teeth right now. I sent her the Pharmacy Checker for Nuvaring for $83 for 3 rings ie. 3 months. That''s cheaper than the $125 or so she''s paying now. She wants the wellness benefits for the kids as well. She will talk with her accountant to handle the new bus in the best way with taxes and x-husband, etc. She''s all set for now and super appreciative.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-11-05 17:11:38', '2025-11-05 17:11:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172993213', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000002095005', 'Dustin Spencer', NULL, '11-5-25 Dustin is the same with a slight increase in income to $23K with his own business. No health changes or anything. He chose the following and knows to call in 10 biz days to set up his payment with the number I gave him. He''s not worried about the network. This is the most affordable with the best benefits this year in his price range.<br><span><br></span><p style="background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);"><b>Enrolled member(s):</b></span><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);background-color:rgb(232, 241, 212);">Dustin Spencer</span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><br></span></p><p style="display:flex;"><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);"><b>Anthem Silver Pathway Essentials 5500 $0 Select Drugs</b></span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Family Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Primary Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Deductible</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Individual Out-of-Pocket Max</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Specialist Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$0</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">$1,400</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">Urgent Care Coinsurance</span></p><p style=""><span style="color:rgb(43, 49, 60);">N/A</span></p><p style="display:flex;background-color:rg