  ('zcrm_1579374000172104139', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000162279001', 'Allison Leach', NULL, '10/20/25<br>Allison called because she wanted to know how her preventative services are covered. I explained that she should have the provider submit claims directly to the p.o box AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-10-20 13:47:22', '2025-10-20 13:47:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172108062', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000171769002', 'Tammy Barrow', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation prior to enrollment citing a change of mind.  I will process &amp; refund Enrollment Fee.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-10-20 13:30:58', '2025-10-20 13:30:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172097089', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000172068008', 'Christopher Price', 'Member & Family $2500 IUA Secure HSA', 'TAX ID/EIN:  20-5236538<br><br>10/20- Request sent to member &amp; advisor via em. Member submitted form to update Tax ID after hours.  I will process.', 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2025-10-20 13:30:53', '2025-10-21 06:24:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172127001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000054820050', 'Michael Brisbane', NULL, '10.20.25 Requested ID card ARM. JA', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2025-10-20 13:15:55', '2025-10-20 13:15:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172125006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000176740001', 'Loyal George', NULL, '10-20-25 Julie is 59 and her husband''s legal name is Loyal but he goes by Berkeley and is 56.  Julie is self-employed as a realtor and appraiser. She will be ending as an <span style="color:rgb(51, 51, 51);">appraiser</span> in 2026 but still a realtor.   Julie was recently changed from  having osteoporosis to osteopenia. She takes HRT and gets meds through GoodRX. They are sorting out how long their current coverage will last either through Nov. or longer. They believe Cobra will be about $1000 per person! They live in Fraser but come to the Front Range for their medical needs. Looking towards Dec. or Jan. 1st start date. Julie did have a polyp removed during her colonoscopy a year ago and then had to pay for the entire procedure bc changed from screening to diagnostic. She was thrilled to learn if that were to happen again it will fall under a new Need with the IUA. She doesn''t need another one for 4 more years from now. They are healthy and really only use plan for wellness screenings. No tobacco. No other issues or meds. They are both very detail oriented and just wanted to understand the process for submitting Needs. They are good with it. Sounds like they''re leaning towards the $1000/$1250 IUA for 2025 and 2026.  They know of the $125/$25. I need to ask them again who referred them to me!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-10-20 13:08:10', '2025-10-20 13:09:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172104134', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000131246003', 'Derek Menold', NULL, '10/20/25<br>Derek requested his 1094 c AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-10-20 13:04:48', '2025-10-20 13:04:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172108057', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000172092013', 'Manuel Alejandro Sanchez Vega', NULL, 'Member &amp; Sp $2500 IUA Care +', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-10-20 13:00:18', '2025-10-20 13:00:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172097081', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011881658', 'James Lynch', NULL, 'Member called in regarding the email cancellation form that he received about Aging into Medicare and the cancellation survey link that he was completing.  He had an issue with the form about checking the last box on the form that states: "<span style="color:rgb(35, 70, 82);background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);">I understand that upon cancellation, any open or ongoing sharing requests will no longer be eligible for sharing.", because he currently has some open needs (labs, appt and a petscan) that he is concerned about coverage for.  He wanted that box to read the date that the sharing would no longer be covered.  He felt that was a very open-ended box to check and was concerned about his open needs being met.  I told him the forthcoming question on that form is to enter the cancellation date (in his case 11/1/25).  That date would correspond to the box above it that he would have to check regarding the sharing of open needs.  He did not seem to be satisfied with that and wanted us to send him an email confirmation of the exact date that the sharing requests would not be eligible for sharing.   He also went on to explain that he feels uncomfortable based on the mix up with the billing back in March/May? a few months back, and that he has not been paying anything for the services, due to the error.  After speaking with Patti, she recommended me to tell him to contact Sedera directly to review this situation for him.  He told me that he is going to reach out to Analisa Cleland via email about this to see if she can give him the confirmation he wants before submitting the cancellation survey form.  I again told him to reach out to Sedera directly, as well. He also inquired about the paragraph in that letter that pertains to retaining the online services option going forward, wanting to know if it would be a good fit for him.  I told him to address that as well with Analisa.  He was good with that.  </span>', 'Michele R', 'Michele R', '2025-10-20 12:54:22', '2025-10-20 12:58:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000172104129', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000168238002', 'Linda Kenny', NULL, '10/20/25<br>Linda called to see how she can get reimbursed. I advised her to have the pharmacy refund her and have them submit the bill AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-10-20 12:53:06', '2025-10-20 12:53:06'),
