  ('zcrm_1579374000171346167', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000161777426', 'Erika Gibson Mull', NULL, '9-29-25 Erika never got her Cobra letter from her former employer to show her SEP. However in June she started a new job and they did not offer benefits. Prior to June she worked as a 1099 contract worker. But, June 15th or so, she changed to a W2 employee and worked PT. We used that as her SEP. She earned $2800 in July and then $6000 in Aug. So, we needed to change her income from $3000 month to $4000 a month which was $30K after some deductions to $48K now. She was paying on $1 before and now will be paying $131.96. She knows if she earns more than expected she needs to adjust the income or expect to pay a % amount back when she files her taxes.   She was very nice and knows she should have stayed on top of this better.  Her current APTC is $424.41.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-09-29 16:41:37', '2025-09-29 16:41:37'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000171346162', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000171119022', 'Ashley Coburn', NULL, '9-29-25 I called Cigna Broker Services and spoke with Jamal. Submitted Ashley''s Binde Payment and Auto-Pay for her plan starting Oct. 1st, $393.92. First payment will be charged today and next will be charged around the 5th of Nov. and each month thereafter. The account is complete in ICHRA Systems as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-09-29 15:29:38', '2025-09-29 15:29:38'),
