  ('zcrm_1579374000170966013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000125475002', 'Sara Tessitore', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation eff 10/1 citing financial reasons.  I will process.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-09-19 10:09:32', '2025-09-19 10:09:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000170966006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000170773001', 'Chandon Williams', 'Decline of Enrollment Fee', '9/19-1st notice sent to member &amp; advisor via em &amp; vm<br>9/22-<span style="color:rgb(49, 57, 73);background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);">Member submitted Payment Update Form.  I will process and re-run enrollment fee of $125 that declined on 9/19   MR and 1st month share amount of $256 with new Bank info</span>', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2025-09-19 09:50:50', '2025-09-22 09:46:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000170975001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021624144', 'Kim Merryweather', NULL, '9/18/25<br>The member called to confirm whether we had updated her address. Upon review, it appeared that she had not submitted a Change Form, so I resent the form to her for completion.<br>During the call, the member inquired whether an endoscopy and colonoscopy would be covered as preventive care, noting that she has Barrett’s disease. I explained that while colonoscopies <i>can</i> be covered under preventive care depending on the context, an <b>endoscopy is not considered preventive</b> under ACA guidelines.<br>The member became frustrated and stated that the procedure is preventive in her case, as it helps prevent cancer. I reiterated that <b>preventive coverage is determined based on the ACA guidelines</b>, and endoscopies are not included under those preventive services.<br>At this point, she disclosed that she has been diagnosed and needs both procedures, and that a small polyp had already been removed. I informed her that once a diagnosis is made or a polyp has been removed, the procedures are no longer classified as <i>screening</i> but instead as <b>diagnostic</b>, which affects how they are processed for coverage.<br>I clarified the difference between preventive, routine, and diagnostic services, as they each fall under different categories of coverage. She remained frustrated, so I asked her to review her medical records to confirm whether a polyp was indeed removed. I also informed her that if the procedure is not eligible under preventive care, she may need to <b>open a medical need sharing request</b> as an alternative route for coverage.<br> AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-09-19 09:16:51', '2025-09-19 09:16:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000170971006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000100501002', 'Zarah Avadisian', NULL, '09/19/2025<br>Answered he is email asking how to login. Asked him what exactly he is trying to accomplish so i can assist.<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-09-19 08:54:55', '2025-09-19 08:54:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000170971001', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000134767002', 'Kara Weld', NULL, '09/19/2025<br>Worked with IT to help explain to Kara exactly how to log in everyone to the app and how to utilize the services for people over 18 and under 18. Going back and fourth through email to try and help her get everyone logged in and ready to use it.<br>AJ', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-09-19 08:51:32', '2025-09-19 08:51:32'),
