  ('zcrm_1579374000169948652', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000170144016', 'Christopher Harding', NULL, '8-20-25 Chris knows to get the Cobra letter for our next meeting as well.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-20 23:24:52', '2025-08-20 23:24:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169948616', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000170144016', 'Christopher Harding', NULL, '8-20-25 Chris is 63, wife is 51 and daughter is 14. They live in C. Springs and were referred to me by Dave at Colorado Springs Insurance. (I''m not sure who that is.)  Chris'' wife is retiring from the school system and if they choose Cobra it will be $2500 for Kaiser. They want to keep Kaiser, if possible. They are healthy and active. His wife is playing pickle ball 3x today. Wife lost  insurance on July 31st. So, he wants a Sept. 1st start date. I sent him the instructions to create the C4 account and select me as agent. We will meet on Monday. I sent him the two Gold plans. This looks the best <span style="color:rgb(77, 77, 79);">KP Colorado Option Gold</span><br><span style="color:rgb(77, 77, 79);">HMO/Gold. He wants Enbrel which is insanely expensive $2K per shot and he got or needs 4 which is $8K. Through Kaiser with his current insurance it will cost him $9K!  The CO Option Gold plan has $600 for specialty meds but it might not cover this one still!  I can''t tell since the delivery method seems different.  Their income will be about $60K each, ie. $120K and they will get an APTC of $1164. So, the price for them is about $795.37. </span><br><span style="color:rgb(77, 77, 79);">UPDATE 8-25-25- He forgot to mention his rental income so his tax credit went down to $912.25 and price up to $1047.12. I''m guessing perhaps $10-$20K more in rental income.</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-20 23:23:02', '2025-08-25 11:50:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169948606', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000169903017', 'Ariel Lovely', NULL, '8-20-25 Ariel is turning 26 this weekend and will be removed from her parents plan. She working for Jeff Childs at Rocky Mountain Kennels. He will pay up to $250 for her membership. She''s healthy, young and doesn''t tend to do the wellness visits.  Her mom Cynthia joined us an I explained it all to both of them. Cynthia was very engaged and seems to grasp it well. Ariel didn''t say much. She has no health issues, no meds and no smoking. She chose Care+ since that''s the most affordable and best option for her age. She enrolled today with her mom''s help. Her mom used  a cc but will change it to ACH for the next billing period. I later realized I should have waived the $100 enrollment fee rather then later sending it to Jeff. We don''t have Jeff''s information to pay him. Patti will refund the $100 tomorrow and I will let Cynthia know to look for the refund. She will be happy. Membership will begin Sept. 1st. I let them know to sign up for the Welcome call as well. All set for now!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-20 23:08:13', '2025-08-21 00:22:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169948601', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000169950023', 'Michelle Maziar', NULL, '8-20-25 Michelle is 45 and lives in GA. She was referred by Shoshana Kressler. She''s getting a subsidy now and is only paying $70. But, she expects her income to go up and subsidy to go down by 2026. She really wants mental health counseling, acupuncture, chiropractic care and physical therapy. She wants somatic therapy and will definitely benefit from the supplement discounts. She''s choosing CARE+. She doesn''t need the mammogram for another year or so and not needing the colonoscopy. She also still has her ACA plan for those items, if she needs. She chose Care+ $1000/$273. She really wanted HAB but it''s not available. Her boyfriend also wants some good mental health counseling but wants it in person, not virtual. She''s going to try it out first.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-20 23:06:21', '2025-08-20 23:06:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169948593', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000124369011', 'Rachel Weitz', NULL, '8-20-25 Rachel was has been getting treated for breast cancer with Zion and it''s been going well but a lot of work. She''s been happy with them. But, now they are ending her treatment as she "manages" the cancer. The "standard of care" is for her to get some shots which will shut down her ovaries. She did some experimental treatments and Zion has been amazing until now. These shots are called Zoladex and are very expensive. She''s applying for a grant from the manufacturer and their income is at a level where they might be granted the money but time will tell. She wanted to get onto C4 but doesn''t have a life change event. Her next shot has been authorized by Zion which will be in Oct. I think she said she needs them every 3 months.She''s getting this shot through the extra sharing fund. She''s been recommended to get a colonoscopy and they don''t share in that either, even though it''s been recommended by her cancer Dr. I gave her the information to get the colonscopy for about $1595 in Lone Tree which still may be cheaper than with reg insurance. She might be able to wait until Jan. to get it. She''ll find out. She was in good spirits but wanted to understand her options.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-20 22:57:52', '2025-08-20 22:57:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169936198', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003401007', 'Benjamin Lampert II', NULL, '8/20/25<br>sent email to let alison know we have recived the bill for her labs AC', 'Concierge', 'Concierge', '2025-08-20 17:49:37', '2025-08-20 17:49:37'),
