  ('zcrm_1579374000169687004', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000169685002', 'Rodney Howell', 'Enrolled in Secure HSA. w/1000 IUA', 'Billing set up outlined in message below. Rodney and Jenny own a business with her sister Jessica Jacobson who is also a lead here in Zoho that will enroll later on for a 10-1 start.  We will combine and convert to a list bill at that time.', 'Kirk Bennett', 'Kirk Bennett', '2025-08-14 17:13:45', '2025-08-14 17:13:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169675033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000163360001', 'Blythe Burge', NULL, '8-14-25 I left a vm for Buffy bc she submitted a quote request for Premium Care $5K IUA.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-14 16:14:15', '2025-08-14 16:14:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169675028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000169680002', 'Andrew Chapman', NULL, '8-14-25 My other notes are under Nicole Duke for Andrew. They are connected but not married, possibly dating. He''s enrolling in Premium Care $1000/$299. His only pre-x is some labs were off such as his PSA and it''s now back to normal. He put it on his app. He understands the pre-x clause and tiered sharing as time progresses. He''s 52 and lives in Boulder. He was referred by Nicole Duke and Nicole was referred by Jessica Hall Muniz.  He inquired about vision benefits but decided against it when I told him what''s included and the price. He asked about some labs which I priced out for him and they were super cheap like $6-$7, $13.80, etc. He was so surprised that he could just choose what he wants and get them ordered with the help of the MPB Concierge Team. He was blown away by how affordable they are. That helped him choose Premium Care instead of Premium HSA. He''s all set for a Sept. 1st start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-14 15:48:52', '2025-08-14 16:23:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169675016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000165358007', 'Sean Fenelon', NULL, '8-14-25 Sean and his wife are in a financially difficult place right now. Once he included the Secure HSA membership his income went down which he wasn''t expecting. If he cancels then his income will go back to where he was expecting. He said he''ll join his wife''s plan but I don''t think this is true. He admitted they just can''t afford it right now and needs to money in his paycheck. He doesn''t like the self-pay aspect. I let him know with his wife''s plan he will likely have a significantly higher ded and mop. Doens''t matter since he can''t afford any of it.  He completed the cancellation form and I have to notify 1Dental next.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-14 14:59:43', '2025-08-14 14:59:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169675011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000123690002', 'Sheala Smith', NULL, '8-14-25 Sheala is trying to decide if she wants to move her kids to her husband''s employer plan. I sent her the prices options and this is what she decided, <br><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">"Thanks, Wendy! I am going to leave everything as is. I appreciate you getting back to me."</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-14 14:36:58', '2025-08-14 14:36:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000169675006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000004455005', 'Carleen Andersen', NULL, '8-14-25 <span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);"> Hey Wendy,</span><br><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">I actually called Cigna yesterday and explained that I accidentally cancelled it through C4HC and they immediately reinstated my plan but, for some reason, they did not let Cigna know that it was back. Cigna told me to give them 72 hours to receive a document from C4HC that says I’m still covered. I’d like to just keep the current plan for now, and possibly look at other options during open enrollment. Hopefully they don’t drag their feet and I can get it figured out quickly. I’ll keep you posted. Thank you so much for your help! It’s appreciated. </span><br><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">Best,</span><br><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);"><br></span><span style="color:rgb(34, 34, 34);">Carleen Andersen</span>', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2025-08-14 14:34:03', '2025-08-14 14:34:03'),
